101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (International recruitment is no longer a seasonal activity a school can run in the margins of a registrar's week. It has become a strategic function, and like the other functions a school chooses not to build from scratch, it rewards being run properly more than being run in-house.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The shift it asks for is one of posture: from filling places to finding and enrolling the right pupils. Pupils who fit a particular school, thrive within it, contribute to its boarding community and support the academic, cultural and nationality balance the school wants. BEP is designed to recruit and evidence that fit rather than chase volume for its own sake.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (British Enrolment Partners is your international enrolment function, outsourced and integrated. It coordinates the whole journey into one joined-up process, from recruitment strategy and market research through to arrival and settling, for every international pupil and whoever introduced them. There is no exclusivity and no two-track system: your existing agents and their commission structures stay exactly as they are, and BEP coordinates across all of them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (For a school without an international function, BEP is that function. For a school with a team, BEP scaffolds it. Built and run by operators who have set up and turned around British boarding schools, it is the function itself, run or supported for you, with the school retaining control of admissions decisions and pupil fit at all times.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
