118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (International recruitment has quietly become a strategic function, but in most schools it still sits in the margins of a registrar's or a head's week, alongside everything else they carry. That mismatch creates a familiar pattern.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (There is rarely a dedicated specialist or a presence on the ground in priority markets, so relationships are built in bursts and then go quiet between visits. There is rarely the time to travel, coordinate agents and follow up every contact from a fair, so effort leaks away after the event that paid for it. And there is rarely the budget or the system to see the whole pipeline, so decisions are made without the visibility they deserve.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (None of this reflects a lack of ambition. It reflects a function that has outgrown the way schools are set up to run it.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
